WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.100
A cell extract holds thousands of different proteins.

2
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:09.520
How can you follow just one?

3
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.240
First, sort by size.

4
00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:15.400
This step is called SDS-PAGE.

5
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:19.200
Heat the extract in SDS, a detergent.

6
00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:25.760
It unfolds each protein and coats it with negative charge, roughly in proportion to

7
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:30.040
its length. Pull the mixture through a gel with an electric field.

8
00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:33.380
Small proteins travel farther than large ones.

9
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.100
Next, find. This step is the western blot.

10
00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:42.500
Move the sorted proteins from the gel onto a membrane.

11
00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:46.900
Then soak the membrane in an antibody against your protein.

12
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:51.840
A second antibody carries an enzyme that makes light or colour.

13
00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:54.440
It marks where the first one stuck.

14
00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:57.020
You see a band at one size.

15
00:00:57.883 --> 00:01:04.023
One antibody is raised against a short piece of a protein with a phosphate on one

16
00:01:04.023 --> 00:01:09.343
residue. It is chosen so that it binds only when the phosphate is present.

17
00:01:10.263 --> 00:01:15.543
A blot with it reads one site, from cells, minutes after a signal arrives.

18
00:01:16.683 --> 00:01:20.563
Blot the same samples with an antibody to the whole protein as well.

19
00:01:21.183 --> 00:01:24.863
Otherwise you cannot tell more phosphate from more protein.

20
00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:27.747
An antibody has limits.

21
00:01:28.507 --> 00:01:33.687
It answers the question you built it for, so it cannot find a site nobody suspected.

22
00:01:34.607 --> 00:01:39.687
It reports that a band got darker, not what fraction of the molecules carry the

23
00:01:39.687 --> 00:01:43.687
phosphate. The antibody can bind the wrong protein.

24
00:01:44.127 --> 00:01:49.167
So a careful blot includes a sample in which the protein or the phosphate is

25
00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:52.867
missing. And a blot averages millions of cells.
